Subject: Cantor Semantic Inspection Wire P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] a6d2699b-213f-47da-999f-3c72cce48077
@ [specification_uuid] 1bddf5c8-35b7-4b29-a833-921048a21410

& [Need]
  + the published semantic transaction is callable from Rust but a future host still lacks one governed machine envelope for success refusal limits and exact replay
  + defining that protocol before executable I/O prevents each adapter from inventing incompatible error and trust semantics

& [Choice]
  + wrap the exact nested request and result instead of flattening or translating semantic fields
  + represent every governed outer or nested refusal as one mutually exclusive bounded fault response
  + validate by complete deterministic replay rather than trusting a digest alone

& [Tradeoff]
  + the wire request repeats the supplied project and intentionally favors portable proof over session efficiency
  + an actual user-facing executable still requires a later narrow authority decision for input output framing and process disposition

& [Authority]
  + implementation authority is limited to CSIW-001 through CSIW-024 and CSIW-A01 through CSIW-A05
